<article class="env-lemma" id="0DS6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DS6">Lemma <span data-tag="0DS6">107.5.24</span>.</a> Let $f: \mathcal{T} \to \mathcal{X}$ be a locally of finite type morphism of Jacobson, pseudo-catenary, and locally Noetherian algebraic stacks which is quasi-DM, whose source is irreducible and whose target is quasi-separated, and let $\mathcal{Z} \hookrightarrow \mathcal{X}$ denote the scheme-theoretic image of $\mathcal{T}$. Then $\dim \mathcal{Z} \leq \dim \mathcal{T}$, and furthermore, exactly one of the following two conditions holds: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
for every finite type point $t \in |T|,$ we have $\dim _ t(\mathcal{T}_{f(t)}) > 0,$ in which case $\dim \mathcal{Z} < \dim \mathcal{T}$; or 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathcal{T}$ and $\mathcal{Z}$ are of the same dimension. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      As was observed in the preceding remark, the dimension of a quasi-DM stack is always non-negative, from which we conclude that $\dim _ t \mathcal{T}_{f(t)} \geq 0$ for all $t \in |\mathcal{T}|$, with the equality 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \dim _ t \mathcal{T}_{f(t)} = \dim _ t \mathcal{T} - \dim _{f(t)} \mathcal{Z}  \]
</div>
    <p>
       holding for a dense open subset of points $t\in |\mathcal{T}|$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>